[-] bumpy		<-->	a++	[250603][001]	./ˈbʌmpi/-NAmE /ˈbʌmpi/
(comparative bumpier, superlative bumpiest)
	;gồ ghề -- (1) (of a surface) not even; with a lot of bumps
		;a bumpy road/track
		;He rode over the bumpy ground on his mountain bike.
		;Extra Examples:
		;The road was getting bumpier and we had to hold on to our seats.
		;She felt quite sick from the long drive over the bumpy road.
	; -- (2) (of a journey) uncomfortable with a lot of sudden unpleasant movements caused by the road surface, weather conditions, etc.
		;a bumpy ride/flight
		;a very bumpy ride through country lanes
	;;























[-] carp		<-->	n++	[250603][001]	./kɑːp/-NAmE /kɑːrp/
[countable, uncountable]
(plural carp)
	;cá chép -- (1) a large freshwater fish that is used for food
		;see also koi
		;Word Origin
	;;












[-] carp		<-->	verb++	[250603][001]	./kɑːp/-NAmE /kɑːrp/
[intransitive]
	;phàn nàn -- (1) to keep complaining about somebody/something in an annoying way
		;I’ve had enough of him constantly carping and criticizing.
		;carp (on) (at somebody) (about somebody/something) Lord, how you carp on, Lucy!
		;Word Origin
	;;













[-] reinstate		<-->	verb++	[250603][001]	./ˌriːɪnˈsteɪt/-NAmE /ˌriːɪnˈsteɪt/
	;khôi phục -- (1) ​reinstate somebody/something (in/as something) to give back a job or position that had been taken away from somebody
		;He was reinstated in his post.
	; -- (2) reinstate something (in/as something) to return something to its previous position or status
		;synonym restore
		;There have been repeated calls to reinstate the death penalty.
		;Tennis has now been reinstated as an Olympic sport.
	;;












[-] underway		<-->	a++	[250603][001]	./ˌʌndəˈweɪ/-NAmE /ˌʌndərˈweɪ/
(also under way)
[not before noun]
	;đang tiến hành -- (1) having started
		;Preparations are well underway for a week of special events in May.
	;;












